ontent_hash":"9a3118cac604ba48fb9bb67e34ab99228fab03fee600a48e9f7f8a782cb3e3df","event_uuid":"5c6e55c4-90ba-4ede-9538-0bb955fd4c7f","position":{"commit_sha":"a532ae9e50e6be3001826b4674b915015118f776","position":"1787959504644397001-5c6e55c4-90ba-4ede-9538-0bb955fd4c7f"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"355cacec3a3a31d6eafa21db99345e56cd2e7812bc593e1e1ab6b84562ab56bc","event_uuid":"06cb46d8-4104-4467-9ca9-57c45468a507","position":{"commit_sha":"71167443ffc047f3489ef967625281cdbe565f4d","position":"1787959536535400001-06cb46d8-4104-4467-9ca9-57c45468a507"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"25beb0ec7f88f7ac72649dff49f790688f1f8ee7992ebdecb2970fe2ba4bb2c7","event_uuid":"037fc90d-4a3e-4f02-9746-b3b19fa63e95","position":{"commit_sha":"62f062f820bca79e3fdde751a3f0be17d550a965","position":"1787960185791905001-037fc90d-4a3e-4f02-9746-b3b19fa63e95"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"f9a57aed665ccaa3b9191e6b7a654d74b4713e548968596a476c20db85998243","event_uuid":"92946e90-0d38-41e5-8f7b-3cd2a74814c1","position":{"commit_sha":"15df2c57398ad9ce18cd9cc505c662bb300cbd9e","position":"1787960876442349001-92946e90-0d38-41e5-8f7b-3cd2a74814c1"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## Phase 1 RCA (rebar-debug) — PROVEN, cited; disposition ESCALATE (no code changed)\n\n**Proven root cause.** `_reads._tracker()` (`src/rebar/_reads.py:42`) uses `if not\nos.path.isdir(tracker)` as its SOLE initialization predicate. A directory that exists but is\nnot a usable store satisfies `isdir`, so the guard never fires and the read proceeds; one layer\ndown the reducer's `except OSError: return results` swallows the failure and yields `[]`. The\ncaller cannot tell \"empty store\" from \"broken store\".\n\n**Runtime confirmation (this worktree, off origin/main `dddaa60`).** Drove the real\n`rebar.list_tickets(repo_root=…)` entry point:\n- Case 1 (production shape) — tracker dir with a `reviewbot-ensure-tickets` marker file and NO\n  `.git`: returned `[]` (should raise `store_uninitialized`).\n- Case 3 (mid-clone) — `.git` present but HEAD unresolvable (`git rev-parse --verify HEAD` rc\n  128): returned `[]` (should raise `store_uninitialized`).\n- Control — an `init_repo` store (has `.git` + resolvable HEAD, zero tickets) reads `[]`\n  correctly, and must keep doing so (`tests/unit/test_reads_uninitialized_store.py`).\n\n**Why it is a defect (cited authority).**\n- The write side already guards usability: `event_prepare._ensure_initialized`\n  (`src/rebar/_store/event_prepare.py:101`) raises when `not isdir(tracker) or not\n  exists(tracker/.git)`. Reads check only `isdir`, so read/write disagree about the same store.\n- `docs/mcp-reference.md` forbids fallback-masking (faults must surface as errors, not resolve\n  to a silent fallback); a broken store reading `[]` is exactly that.\n- The existing contract test pins the distinction (\"directory does not exist\" = error vs\n  \"exists and holds no tickets\" = `[]`).\n- Standing intent is documented by prior closed tickets: `antelopine-limivorous-chinchilla`\n  (introduced the guard + the `store_uninitialized` code), `fathomable-yester-thrip` (recorded\n  this as a residual), and `unfit-beneficial-whimbrel` AC3 (\"while the clone is in flight,\n  tracker reads report `store_uninitialized` rather than `[]`\" — explicitly left unticked,\n  pointing here).\n\n**Defect origin / `caused_by`.** Attributed to `44fd-230c-5893-4246`\n(`antelopine-limivorous-chinchilla`), introducing commit `84fc5f9b68df8` (the line\n`if not os.path.isdir(tracker):`). That change added the read guard but keyed it on directory\npresence only, not store usability — an incomplete implementation of the guard's own intent\n(and of parity with the write side, which already checked `.git`). `caused_by` link recorded.\nClass if closed: `plan_defect` / incomplete-implementation.\n\n**Caller-dependency gate.** Only consumer of the `store_uninitialized` code is\n`rebar.audit.server._audited_tickets` (`src/rebar/audit/server.py:99-102`), which catches that\ncode and degrades to an empty index while propagating every OTHER error. Extending the guard to\nemit `store_uninitialized` for broken/mid-clone stores keeps that caller consistent (it degrades\nrather than 500s). No high-confidence behavioral-dependency caller relies on the current `[]`.\n\n**Why ESCALATE rather than auto-land.** This is a genuine defect with documented standing\nintent, but the correct fix is NOT behavior-preserving and carries a design choice, so under the\norchestrator's escalation rules it needs human authorization:\n1. It changes observable read semantics **repo-wide** — all 7 library/MCP read entry points that\n   funnel through `_tracker()` now raise for a class of inputs that previously returned `[]`.\n   The ticket itself flags this blast radius as the reason it was scoped out of change 2244.\n2. The \"usable store\" predicate is a design tradeoff: `.env-id` is git-ignored LOCAL state\n   (absent immediately after a valid clone — would misclassify a fresh valid clone as\n   uninitialized; cf. `ab61-f3e8-6ee6-4905`), so the read-side discriminator should be a\n   **resolvable git HEAD** (matches AC3 and the mid-clone case), which adds a HEAD-resolution on\n   the read hot path and raises the question of unifying with the write-side check.\n\n**Recommended fix (for the authorizing human).** In `_reads._tracker()`, after the `isdir`\ncheck, also treat the store as uninitialized (same `store_uninitialized` code + wording) when it\nis not a usable store — i.e. `.git` absent OR HEAD not resolvable (`git rev-parse --verify -q\nHEAD`). Keep the existing empty-initialized-store contract test passing unmodified, add regression\ncoverage for (a) present dir without `.git`, (b) `.git` present but HEAD unresolvable (mid-clone),\nand (c) a guard that fails if the predicate reverts to bare `os.path.isdir`. Consider factoring the\nusability predicate so read and write sides share it.","timestamp":1787938141287821001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## Fix-plan detail (moved out of the description to keep it under the P4 admission limit)\n\n**Three init gates, precisely.** `event_prepare._ensure_initialized` (a `.git`-presence check on\nthe low-level append path); `_seam.append_event` at `src/rebar/_commands/_seam.py:555` (the\nAUTHORITATIVE write-command gate, requires `.env-id`; bug roar-nurse-stomp / ab61; pinned by\n`tests/unit/test_store_copy_needs_env_id.py`); and the read chokepoint `_reads._tracker`. The one\nmessage string is emitted from ~14 sites enforcing two different preconditions, so read and write\ndo NOT fully agree by design.\n\n**Why reads deliberately do NOT require `.env-id`.** `.env-id` is git-ignored LOCAL provenance\nstate, absent immediately after a valid clone. Verified in-session: a store with `.git` + a\nresolvable HEAD but no `.env-id` reads its tickets fine, while a write is correctly rejected by\nthe `_seam` `.env-id` gate. So a just-cloned store MUST stay readable; only writes require the\nprovenance stamp. The fix therefore closes the `.git`/HEAD read/write disagreement (broken /\nmid-clone store readable-as-empty) and intentionally leaves the `.env-id` asymmetry alone.\n\n**Write-gate behavior change + safety (addresses plan-review BLOCK rev2).** Sharing the `.git`+HEAD\npredicate means `event_prepare._ensure_initialized` now also rejects a `.git`-present-but-HEAD-\nunresolvable (mid-clone) store. Proven safe for the init/first-write path: instrumenting the call\nshowed `_ensure_initialized` is invoked exactly once across `init_repo` + first `create_ticket`,\nand at that call HEAD already resolves -- init creates the store's initial commits through\n`init_core`, not through the guarded append path. The full write suite is re-run at GREEN to\nconfirm no other write path appends into an unborn-HEAD store.\n\n**Pre-mortem (how could this fail?).** (1) init writes before the first commit -> RULED OUT\n(single `_ensure_initialized` call, HEAD resolves). (2) another write path appends to an\nunborn-HEAD store -> guarded by re-running the full write suite at GREEN. (3) `git` binary absent\n-> the predicate's `subprocess.run` uses `check=False`; a nonzero rc means \"HEAD not resolvable\"\n(not usable), while an OSError (git missing) is a distinct environment failure that propagates\nrather than masquerading as `store_uninitialized`; covered by a test. (4) perf: `git rev-parse`\nper read is negligible -- the read path ALREADY spawns git (throttled `git fetch`/reconverge via\n`_fresh`), so no new process class. (5) walk-up false positive -> the explicit `.git`-exists check\nprecedes the HEAD probe.\n\n**Prior art.** git invoked via `git -C tracker rev-parse --verify -q HEAD`, matching the existing\n`footprint._git` read-probe pattern; the heavier `gitutil.run_git` is deliberately not reused so\nthe read chokepoint does not import the write-core lock machinery and `_reads` stays out of the\nimport SCC.","timestamp":1787958184037142001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## Plan-review rev4 (LLM tier ran) — BLOCK on one G6 finding; resolved in rev5 plan\n\n**Blocking (G6).** \"Widening `store_uninitialized` to fire for broken/mid-clone stores collides\nwith the audit-server consumer, which degrades that exact code to an empty page — silently\nblanking a genuinely broken store, the same masking this change exists to remove.\" Cites\n`src/rebar/audit/server.py:101` and `tests/unit/test_reads_uninitialized_store.py:163`.\n\n**Analysis.** Correct catch. `audit.server._audited_tickets` catches `store_uninitialized` and\ndegrades to an empty index. Its docstring PROMISES \"a genuinely broken store is not silently\nblanked\" — a promise that held only because broken/mid-clone stores used to read `[]` (never\nraised). This fix makes them raise `store_uninitialized`, so they now fall into the caught bucket\nand the docstring's guarantee becomes false. (Behavior at the audit layer is actually unchanged —\nthose stores rendered empty before too — but the module now silently blanks them while claiming it\ndoes not.)\n\n**Resolution (in approved scope — this is the caller-sweep reconciliation the operator asked me to\ncomplete; NOT a new behavior change).** Keep the index rendering empty for any `store_uninitialized`\n(a read-only web index must not 500), but make it HONEST and NON-silent: correct the docstring, and\nbroaden the WARNING log so a present-but-unusable store is logged. Operators diagnose store health\nvia the driving agent / CLI, which now surfaces the absent-vs-unusable distinction. Added\n`src/rebar/audit/server.py` to file_impact and an AUDIT acceptance criterion (renders empty AND\nlogs for a present-but-unusable store; still propagates a non-`store_uninitialized` failure).\n\n**Advisory folded in (T5b).** `store_is_usable`'s git-subprocess failure taxonomy is now explicit:\n`check=False` so a clean non-zero rc == \"HEAD unresolvable\" -> not usable, while an OSError (git\nbinary missing / env failure) PROPAGATES rather than collapsing into `store_uninitialized`. Pinned\nby a new predicate test.\n\nDescription trimmed to <8000 chars (P4). Re-running `review-plan` for a non-BLOCK verdict.","timestamp":1787959536535400001}],"created_at":1787815077692201001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"aa3b3f42-5d08-46fb-8cf0-52abc44521a8","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"b3aa-b77b-cf87-4481"},{"link_uuid":"707c0e3f-6aff-4aaa-ad3f-aed01b350f61","provenance":"explicit","relation":"caused_by","target_id":"44fd-230c-5893-4246"},{"link_uuid":"92946e90-0d38-41e5-8f7b-3cd2a74814c1","relation":"blocks","target_id":"c066-c496-7012-4a39"}],"description":"## Summary\n\n`_reads._tracker` raises `store_uninitialized` only when the tracker directory is ABSENT\n(`src/rebar/_reads.py`, `if not os.path.isdir(tracker)`). A directory that EXISTS but is not a\nusable store — no `.git`, or a `.git` with no resolvable HEAD, or one mid-clone — satisfies\n`isdir`, so every read returns `[]`. The caller cannot distinguish \"this store is empty\" from\n\"this store is broken\", which is the exact confusion the guard was added to remove.\n\n## Encountered three times, each independently\n\n1. **In production.** The deployed MCP server served an EMPTY tracker for an extended period —\n   the store dir held `reviewbot-ensure-tickets` marker files and no `.git`; `isdir` was true so\n   the guard never fired and `rebar.list_tickets()` returned `READ_OK count=0`. Proven on the box.\n2. **`fathomable-yester-thrip` (change 2244, merged).** `clear_tracker_dir` empties CONTENTS but\n   leaves the directory, so between clear and a completed clone reads return `[]`. Recorded there\n   as a residual, not fixed.\n3. **`unfit-beneficial-whimbrel` AC3.** \"While the clone is in flight, tracker reads report\n   `store_uninitialized` rather than `[]`\" — NOT met, same reason; left unticked, points here.\n\n## Why the obvious fixes do not apply\n\nThe MCP deployment's tracker path is itself a MOUNT POINT (`/dev/nvme1n1`, xfs, per `/proc/mounts`),\nso the directory cannot be removed and nothing renamed over it — the entrypoint clears contents,\nnot the directory. The fix has to be on the READ side.\n\n## Constraint the fix must respect\n\nAn EXISTING but empty INITIALIZED store must still read `[]` — that is a real contract with an\nexisting test (`tests/unit/test_reads_uninitialized_store.py`: \"An EXISTING but empty store is\nNOT an error\"). So the discriminator cannot be emptiness. It has to be \"is this a usable\nstore\": a resolvable git HEAD. `.env-id` is ruled out as the read predicate (git-ignored,\nabsent right after a valid clone; cf. `ab61-f3e8-6ee6-4905`).\n\n## Blast radius\n\n`_reads._tracker` funnels 7 read entry points, so this changes core read semantics repo-wide —\nthe reason it was scoped out of 2244.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] A tracker directory that exists but is NOT a usable store reads as `store_uninitialized`,\n      not `[]`.\n- [ ] An existing, empty, INITIALIZED store still reads `[]` — the existing contract test\n      continues to pass unmodified.\n- [ ] A store mid-clone (directory present, HEAD not yet resolvable) reads as uninitialized.\n- [ ] Regression coverage fails if the predicate reverts to a bare `os.path.isdir`.\n\n---\n\n## Fix plan (operator-APPROVED; rebar-debug Phase 2)\n\n**Root cause (proven; full RCA in prior comment).** `_reads._tracker()` gates the read path\non `os.path.isdir(tracker)` only; a dir that exists but has no `.git`, or `.git` with an\nunresolvable HEAD, satisfies `isdir`, so the guard never fires and reads yield `[]`.\nAttributed to `44fd-230c-5893-4246` (commit `84fc5f9b`).\n\n**Approved change.** Broaden the read-side init predicate so a present-but-unusable store raises\n`store_uninitialized` instead of `[]`, across all library/MCP read entry points (the ~7 funneling\nthrough `_reads._tracker`; MCP read tools delegate to these facades). Predicate: `.git` present\nAND `git rev-parse --verify -q HEAD` resolves. The masking removed is the one that misleads a\nDRIVING AGENT on the read path (library/CLI/MCP); the audit web index is a deliberately different\nread-only consumer (see caller gate).\n\n**Gate model (three gates; NOT identical -- see comment).** `event_prepare._ensure_initialized`\n(`.git`), `_seam.append_event` (`.env-id`, authoritative write gate), and `_reads._tracker`.\nReads deliberately do NOT adopt `.env-id` (git-ignored local state absent right after a valid\nclone, which must stay readable). This closes the `.git`/HEAD read/write disagreement only.\n\n**Design.** New stdlib-only leaf `src/rebar/_store/store_usability.py::store_is_usable(tracker)`\n= isdir AND `.git` present AND HEAD resolves (git via `git -C tracker`; `.git`-exists check\nprecedes the HEAD probe so git cannot walk up to the parent code repo). `subprocess.run` uses\n`check=False`: a clean non-zero rc == \"HEAD unresolvable\" -> not usable; an OSError (git binary\nmissing) is a DISTINCT environment failure that PROPAGATES rather than collapsing into\n`store_uninitialized` (advisory T5b; test-pinned). Both `_reads._tracker` and\n`event_prepare._ensure_initialized` call it -- the write gate thereby also rejects a mid-clone\nstore, proven safe for init (see comment). The leaf keeps `_reads` out of the write-core import SCC.\n\n**Files.**\n- `src/rebar/_store/store_usability.py` (new) -- shared `store_is_usable`.\n- `src/rebar/_reads.py` -- `_tracker` raises `store_uninitialized` when `not store_is_usable`.\n- `src/rebar/_store/event_prepare.py` -- `_ensure_initialized` calls the shared predicate.\n- `src/rebar/audit/server.py` -- reconcile the one consumer (docstring + log; behavior unchanged).\n- `tests/unit/test_reads_uninitialized_store.py` -- read + write-gate + predicate + audit regression.\n\n**Caller-dependency gate + reconciliation (addresses plan-review BLOCK G6).** The only consumer\nof `store_uninitialized` is `rebar.audit.server._audited_tickets`, a read-only WEB index whose\ncorrect failure mode is \"render an empty page, not 500\". Under the OLD read semantics a\npresent-but-unusable store read `[]`, so it ALSO rendered empty there -- behavior is unchanged by\nthis fix. BUT that module's docstring promised \"a genuinely broken store is not silently blanked\",\na promise that held only because broken stores did not raise `store_uninitialized`. This fix makes\nthem raise it, so the promise is now false. Reconcile HONESTLY (no behavior change): the index\nstill degrades any `store_uninitialized` (absent OR present-but-unusable) to empty because a\nread-only web index must not 500; correct the docstring to state that; and broaden the WARNING log\nso a present-but-unusable store is LOGGED (not silently blanked) -- operators diagnose store health\nvia the driving agent/CLI, which now surfaces the distinction. No caller depends on the old\n`[]`-for-broken-store on the driving-agent path.\n\n**Acceptance criteria (each evidenced by a test in the named file).**\n- [ ] READ: tracker dir exists but no `.git` -> raises `store_uninitialized`, not `[]`\n      (drive `rebar.list_tickets`; assert `error_code_for(exc) == \"store_uninitialized\"`).\n- [ ] READ: mid-clone (`.git` present, HEAD unresolvable) -> raises `store_uninitialized`.\n- [ ] READ: existing empty INITIALIZED store still reads `[]` (existing contract test unchanged).\n- [ ] READ: valid clone with resolvable HEAD but NO `.env-id` still reads successfully\n      (asserts reads/writes deliberately differ on `.env-id`).\n- [ ] WRITE: `event_prepare._ensure_initialized` rejects a mid-clone store and still accepts an\n      initialized store (covers the write-gate behavior change).\n- [ ] PREDICATE: `store_is_usable` is False for absent/no-`.git`/mid-clone, True for an\n      initialized store and a HEAD-resolvable clone without `.env-id`.\n- [ ] PREDICATE: a missing `git` binary (OSError) PROPAGATES from `store_is_usable` rather than\n      being reported as `store_uninitialized` (T5b failure-taxonomy).\n- [ ] AUDIT: `audit.server._audited_tickets` renders empty (returns `[]`) AND logs a warning for a\n      present-but-unusable store, and still propagates a non-`store_uninitialized` failure.\n- [ ] Regression: reverting the predicate to bare `os.path.isdir` returns broken/mid-clone to RED\n      (defect-seeded mutation check).\n\n**Verification.** RED->GREEN in the named test file: broken/mid-clone READ and write-gate\nmid-clone cases RED pre-fix, GREEN post-fix; empty-init and no-`.env-id`-clone stay `[]`; mutation\nto bare `isdir` returns to RED. Read + write suites stay green.\n\n**Out of approved scope (parity -- discovered tickets):** CLI read path (`reads_cli.py`) and\nother bare-`isdir` read sites -- Step 7 parity sweep.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_store/store_usability.py","reason":"new stdlib-only leaf: shared store_is_usable predicate (isdir AND .git present AND HEAD resolves)"},{"path":"src/rebar/_reads.py","reason":"read chokepoint _tracker raises store_uninitialized when store not usable, across all library/MCP read entry points"},{"path":"src/rebar/_store/event_prepare.py","reason":"write guard _ensure_initialized calls the shared predicate; now also rejects mid-clone (HEAD unresolvable) stores"},{"path":"src/rebar/audit/server.py","reason":"reconcile the sole store_uninitialized consumer: correct docstring + broaden warning log so a present-but-unusable store is logged not silently blanked (behavior unchanged: index still renders empty)"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_reads_uninitialized_store.py","reason":"regression: read broken/mid-clone raise; no-env-id clone still reads; write-gate mid-clone rejected; git-missing OSError propagates; audit renders-empty+logs; store_is_usable predicate; guard-reverts-to-isdir"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["blocks","c066-c496-7012-4a39"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"c8807214-6e53-450c-a555-a17f2afa29e5","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"aefe-614a-2631-4117","ticket_type":"bug","title":"reads return [] for a directory that exists but is not a usable store, so a broken store is indistinguishable from an empty one","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["707c0e3f-6aff-4aaa-ad3f-aed01b350f61","ac453ef7-9a0c-4ecc-af20-2566c03980eb","c8807214-6e53-450c-a555-a17f2afa29e5","e301dbcb-c348-4b82-a360-25dfc0468ada","fbdfd8bb-c3ed-4461-8079-a8b2be1e4808","063f1878-f918-4e72-ac61-e8568203f87d","6c5eabef-dddf-47db-8323-ce324e2f23c6","2c161984-8ca9-4154-8da1-be3825354526","f4bd1d40-f233-438c-b784-7fef7be570b5","613a7142-8fe0-445e-81f2-45f7f86eaf0f","9e6a821d-1dcb-4c17-98fd-c38ce9339a59","aa73a5bf-f92c-4aed-8d9c-c83a5986a206","5c6e55c4-90ba-4ede-9538-0bb955fd4c7f","06cb46d8-4104-4467-9ca9-57c45468a507","037fc90d-4a3e-4f02-9746-b3b19fa63e95","92946e90-0d38-41e5-8f7b-3cd2a74814c1"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787960876442349002,"uuid":"6fdefc4e-c044-4fec-9ba8-4169eeb9efe6"}